--TEST--
`Core\Test::request` throws a `LogicError` for a `clientIp` that is not one address and for a `scheme` other than `http` and `https`, and `Core\Test\Response::error` is `null` for a request that did not fail — `rule:testing/in-process-request`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Test::request, Core\Test\Response::status, Core\Test\Response::error
// A host name, an address with a port and a list of addresses are not one
// address, so each `clientIp` below throws a `LogicError`.
if (Core\Env::context() == Core\Env::Context::Request) {
    if (Core\Request::path() == "/fails") {
        throw new LogicError("no such order");
    }
    echo "ok";
} else {
    array<string> $addresses = ["example.com", "203.0.113.9:80", "203.0.113.9, 198.51.100.7"];
    foreach ($addresses as string $address) {
        try {
            Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/", {clientIp: $address});
        } catch (LogicError $wrongAddress) {
            echo $wrongAddress->message, "\n";
        }
    }
    // Only `http` and `https` are allowed. The check is case-sensitive.
    array<string> $schemes = ["ftp", "HTTPS", ""];
    foreach ($schemes as string $scheme) {
        try {
            Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/", {scheme: $scheme});
        } catch (LogicError $wrongScheme) {
            echo $wrongScheme->message, "\n";
        }
    }
    // An IPv6 address and `https` are allowed. The request did not fail,
    // so `error()` returns `null`.
    var $fine = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/", {clientIp: "2001:db8::1", scheme: "https"});
    echo $fine->status(), " ", $fine->error() ?? "null", "\n";
    var $failed = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/fails");
    echo $failed->status(), " ", $failed->error() ?? "null", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Test::request(): `clientIp` must be one IPv4 or IPv6 address, and `example.com` is not one
Core\Test::request(): `clientIp` must be one IPv4 or IPv6 address, and `203.0.113.9:80` is not one
Core\Test::request(): `clientIp` must be one IPv4 or IPv6 address, and `203.0.113.9, 198.51.100.7` is not one
Core\Test::request(): `scheme` must be "http" or "https", not `ftp`
Core\Test::request(): `scheme` must be "http" or "https", not `HTTPS`
Core\Test::request(): `scheme` must be "http" or "https", not ``
200 null
500 LogicError: no such order
